  "description": "LILXAH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H90 N66 Na2 O2 Sm6,7(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 1 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 1 O neighbors; Sm1F (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm2F (Sm) has 1 O neighbors; Sm3F (Sm) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.670-3.882 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.16-115.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (py)18Sm6O2(N3)16Na2·7(py).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
